{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RegTraceGram","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RegTraceGram","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TraceFormSemisimple","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.BilinearForm","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Basis.Basic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceGram_toMatrix_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceGram_toMatrix_apply","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGram.lean#L77-L84","doc":"**Gram entries are the observable regular-trace values (sorry-free).**\nRecords that the `(i, j)` entry of the Gram matrix in a basis `b` is\n`tr(L_{b_i b_j})`, so a `T_w`-basis Gram computation is literally a\ntable of Markov-trace observables. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.isSemisimpleRing_of_regTraceGram_det_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.isSemisimpleRing_of_regTraceGram_det_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGram.lean#L58-L75","doc":"**Gram-determinant ⟹ semisimple, explicit-matrix form (sorry-free).**\nFor any finite basis `b` of `A`, a nonzero determinant of the regular\ntrace form's Gram matrix `BilinForm.toMatrix b (regTraceBilin K A)`\nforces semisimplicity.  The Gram entries are the observable traces\n`toMatrix b (regTraceBilin) i j = regTraceForm K A (b i) (b j)\n= tr(L_{b_i b_j})` (`BilinForm.toMatrix_apply` ∘ `regTraceBilin_apply`).\n\nThis is the exact hook a `T_w`-basis Gram computation plugs into:\nsupply the basis `b` (brick `qou-lrz1`) and the determinant value\n`det = [n]_q!` (brick `qou-twwf`), and semisimplicity of `H_n(q)`\nfollows — no further Hecke input.  The `n = 2` value is already\ncomputed concretely in `QOU.Hecke.H2CompanionRep`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.isSemisimpleRing_of_regTraceBilin_nondegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.isSemisimpleRing_of_regTraceBilin_nondegenerate","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGram.lean#L48-L56","doc":"**Abstract semisimplicity from the bilinear form's nondegeneracy\n(sorry-free).**  Restates the B3d keystone through `regTraceBilin`,\nso that Mathlib's `nondegenerate_iff_det_ne_zero` — applied to\n`regTraceBilin` — turns semisimplicity into a Gram-determinant\ncondition on any chosen basis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceBilin_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceBilin_apply","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGram.lean#L45-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceBilin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.regTraceBilin","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RegTraceGram.lean#L36-L41","doc":"The **regular trace form as a bilinear form**:\n`B(x, y) = trace(L_{xy})`.  Being a genuine `LinearMap.BilinForm`,\nit plugs into Mathlib's Gram-matrix / determinant API. ","signatureChunk":0}]}